module Proof
  # Turns the words typed after `proof` into a value for each command.
  #
  # The command's interface is `proof.usage.kdl`, and the words a person or an
  # agent types come in as a list of strings. Every use case would have to
  # read flags, spell-check them, and refuse a mistake the same way, and one
  # that read them differently would accept a command line the spec refuses.
  #
  # This module reads the words once. It reads each command's flags from the
  # spec, hands back a typed value for the command, and raises a mistake that
  # says what is wrong. It starts no run, reads no file, and makes no network
  # call.
  module CommandLine
  end
end
